{
  "$schema": "https://www.getbifrost.ai/schema",
  "client": {
    "_comment_drop_excess": "2026-08-10: false -> true. With false, a full provider buffer QUEUES instead of rejecting, so requests sat in Bifrost's buffer for hours (observed: 3.9h on /v1/chat/completions, 231 leaked CLOSE_WAIT sockets, 4300 open FDs). true makes an over-capacity lane return immediately so the caller's fallback chain cascades to a cloud provider. Nothing may queue unbounded.",
    "drop_excess_requests": true,
    "initial_pool_size": 100,
    "enforce_auth_on_inference": true
  },
  "providers": {
    "vllm-local": {
      "keys": [
        {
          "name": "local-noauth",
          "value": "EMPTY",
          "_comment_models": "MUST mirror vllm-chat's --served-model-name list EXACTLY (docker-compose.vllm.yml). Two names were missing until 2026-08-11 — gpt-oss-20b and Qwen3.6-27B resolved fine on a direct :18801 call but 403'd through the gateway, and Legion references gpt-oss-20b ~24x and Qwen3.6-27B ~10x. Every name here answers with Qwen/Qwen3-8B-AWQ as of Pass-6; the names are legacy, not descriptive.",
          "models": [
            "Qwen3.5-35B-A3B",
            "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B",
            "qwen3-chat",
            "Qwen3-32B-AWQ",
            "gpt-oss-20b",
            "Qwen3.6-27B"
          ],
          "weight": 1.0,
          "aliases": {
            "qwen3-chat": "Qwen3.5-35B-A3B",
            "Qwen3-32B-AWQ": "Qwen3.5-35B-A3B",
            "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B": "Qwen3.5-35B-A3B",
            "gpt-oss-20b": "Qwen3.5-35B-A3B",
            "Qwen3.6-27B": "Qwen3.5-35B-A3B"
          }
        }
      ],
      "network_config": {
        "base_url": "http://vllm-chat:8000",
        "default_request_timeout_in_seconds": 90,
        "max_retries": 1
      },
      "custom_provider_config": {
        "base_provider_type": "openai",
        "allowed_requests": {
          "_comment_list_models": "MUST stay false. /v1/models fans out to every provider with list_models=true, so a model-list call joins the inference queue behind real work (Legion's stack_monitor.py documented it hanging past 150s on 2026-08-03, when vllm-chat ran --max-num-seqs 1). vllm-chat now runs --max-num-seqs 6, which makes the hang less likely but NOT impossible — model discovery must never depend on inference capacity, at any concurrency. Corrected 2026-08-11: this comment previously asserted seqs=1 as current fact.",
          "list_models": false,
          "chat_completion": true,
          "chat_completion_stream": true
        }
      },
      "_comment_capacity": "2026-08-11 Pass-6: vllm-chat swapped to Qwen3-8B-AWQ + max-num-seqs 1->6 (V2 UVA blocker sidestepped by VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=0, and vLLM's own budget check reports 'Maximum concurrency for 32,768 tokens per request: 9.38x' so 6 fits with 3.4x headroom). Bifrost concurrency raised 1->6 to match, buffer_size 2->12 (2 x concurrency, standard sizing) so callers don't get 400 drops before vLLM's own queue is engaged. If the 8B slots wedge under sustained real load, drop concurrency back to 1 buffer 2 first (matches vllm --max-num-seqs=1 rollback in shared-infra/.env) before touching anything else.",
      "concurrency_and_buffer_size": {
        "concurrency": 6,
        "buffer_size": 12
      }
    },
